  "description": "LUYDIT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H144 N8 Nd4 O17 S8 2+,2(Cl1 O4 1-),3.33(C3 H7 N1 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.662-5.277 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.85-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C104H144N8Nd4O17S8·2(ClO4)·3.33(dmf)·5(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
